# SDD Protocol Rule

When a request triggers code generation, a new feature, API/provider
integration, strategy change, migration or deployment-affecting change:

1. Check the active ticket and its PRD/plan/tasklist.
2. If required artifacts are missing, prepare or request a minimal spec before
   implementation.
3. Confirm acceptance criteria, write-set, out-of-scope items and tests.
4. Implement only the approved scope with one active Coder.
5. Hand the result to read-only Review, then independent Verification.
6. Update tasklist and memory bank only after verification passes.

For a small documentation-only change, state why the lightweight path is
sufficient and still report changed files and checks.
